module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.adding_a_seed_module_refuses_convergence_on_an_unowned_lib_rs

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread, CeilingAmbiguous }

data adding_a_seed_module_refuses_convergence_on_an_unowned_lib_rs: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "adding_a_seed_module_refuses_convergence_on_an_unowned_lib_rs" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: CeilingAmbiguous },

  receipts: [
    "SPECIMEN (NAMESPACE-XL wave 1, PR #14317, 2026-10-18): the wave made std.host_text a dependency of seed-mirrored modules (std.coercion, gunbc.rust_crate_package_ident, extdeps.version.semver), so a new stage0 module std_host_text entered the seed. After the partition row and the produced mirror were committed, heal-generated-artifacts (`claim_executor --regen-round-cost`) still refused, printing only `convergence kind projection returned unknown closed variant Refused`. Exposing the planner's payload (a local, unpushed edit of v2.workflow.regen_convergence_transaction regen_stage_plan_kind_label) read: SeedMembershipUnresolved { reason: lib.rs has no owner in generated_stage0_crate_partition, surface: RegenSurfaceIdentity { declaring_module: v1.compiler.emit_rust, projected_path: lib.rs } }. The lib.rs the candidate tree held was itself TRANSITIONAL: committing it got past the planner, but once the regenerated partition mirror was installed too, the candidate lib.rs no longer declared std_host_text (a partition crate owns it) and lib.rs returned to main's bytes -- so the planner refused twice on two different lib.rs states before either was the fixed point.",
    "WHAT ONE NEW SEED MODULE COST, IN ORDER, each a separate heal round and each a generator output installed outside the job that owns it: (1) the partition row (v2.workflow.rust_crate_partition) and the regenerated partition file; (2) the produced mirror std_host_text.rs (`emitted surface has no committed mirror`); (3) a transitional lib.rs (SeedMembershipUnresolved, above); (4) the partition file's own mirror gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs (`WholeCompilerRebuildRequired partition_generation_authority=[...]`); (5) lib.rs again, back to main's bytes; (6) the partition crate src/v1/stage0_std_core/src/lib.rs from `claim_executor --emit-partition-crates --write` (E0432 unresolved crate::std_host_text in the seed build). Every one is derivable from the partition row alone; heal derives none of them in one round.",
    "DEFECT 1 -- INVALID STATE: lib.rs, the stage0 crate's module list, is a seed surface the convergence planner must classify, but no row of gunbc.stage0.stage0_crate_partition_generated owns it, so the host derives UnresolvedSeedMembership for it (src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs, the `has no owner in generated_stage0_crate_partition` arm) and v2.workflow.regen_convergence_transaction regen_first_unresolved refuses the whole stage. Any change that adds or removes a seed module changes lib.rs, so EVERY such PR refuses convergence and needs lib.rs installed by hand from the candidate tree. HARM: the heal job cannot converge a routine seed-module addition; authors install generated files outside the job that owns them.",
    "DEFECT 2 -- INVALID STATE: the host's projection of the planner outcome (required_regen_host.rs, the `convergence kind projection returned unknown closed variant <value>` arm, reading regen_stage_plan_kind_label) renders RegenStagePlanningRefused as the bare word `Refused`, dropping the RegenConvergenceRefusal payload that names the refusal and its surface. HARM: a typed, located refusal reaches CI as an unlocated one; the specimen cost three remote regen runs to read a reason the model already carried. This is DESIGN section 5's `every degradation is typed, located and countable` lost at the last link.",
    "DEFECT 3 -- INVALID STATE: the heal step `Refuse when the stage0 round wrote a file the seed-build writer owns` (dag/gunbc/heal_candidate_stage0.dag heal_stage0_overlap_refusal_wet) crashed in its own evaluation on #14317 at 7bf0694203a (2026-10-18): `error: evaluating heal_stage0_overlap_refusal_wet ... cause: NoSuchVariable { name: \"value\" }`. Its refusal message is built only on the drifted arm, from `map(drifted, d => d.entry.path.value as String)`, so the path it should name -- the seed-build roster file it found drifted -- never reaches CI. HARM: a typed, located refusal (`HealStage0RoundWroteSeedBuildArtifact`, naming the paths) becomes an evaluator crash with no subject; the author cannot tell which file, or whether the refusal fired at all. CEILING: structurally guaranteed (the refusal's rendering is total over its own carrier and is exercised by a control). NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the overlap refusal renders every drifted path through an accessor the evaluator resolves, proved by a control that feeds a non-empty drifted population and expects the named paths in the reason.",
    "DEFECT 3 ROOT CAUSE, FOUND (2026-10-18, by bisecting #14317's 83 .dag changes on a 64 GB runner): the overlap step's crash was NOT the heal tool's -- it was THIS ROW. An earlier wording of the DEFECT 2 receipt quoted the host's format string with its placeholder in braces, and a braced identifier inside a .dag string literal is interpolation, so evaluating this module (which the overlap step's closure loads) looked up a variable named value and failed. Restoring this one file made the step exit 0; restoring any other changed file did not. The placeholder is now written with angle brackets. The step's crash therefore says nothing about heal_stage0_overlap_refusal_wet's own rendering, and DEFECT 3 above is withdrawn as a heal defect. What it does show is a separate hazard: a ledger row's prose can break an unrelated tool's evaluation, and the failure names the variable, not the file.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable for both -- the refusal is loud (the job fails), and a by-hand install of generator output works around defect 1; nothing mechanical prevents either. CEILING: structurally guaranteed for defect 1 (every seed surface the planner sees has an owner or a declared bootstrap role, so UnresolvedSeedMembership is unreachable for lib.rs) and for defect 2 (the planner's refusal crosses to the host as a typed value that the host renders whole).",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGERS, AS CAPABILITIES. Defect 1: the convergence planner classifies the stage0 crate's lib.rs (and any other crate-root surface the emitter writes) with a declared role and seed membership, so a PR that adds a seed module converges in heal with no hand-installed file -- proved by a fixture that adds one module and expects a planned stage, not a refusal. Defect 2: the host renders a RegenStagePlanningRefused outcome with its full RegenConvergenceRefusal payload (variant, reason, surface), proved by a control that feeds the projection a refusal and expects the payload in the printed reason. Routed by tidy-ant-251 to Manager 2."
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
